\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {20}{\ignorespaces Theorem\nonbreakingspace \ref {thm:light} at $(3,2)$, with $g_3$ the light vector. Left, upstairs: the unit circle, which $g_3$ lies inside, and the ellipse $u^{\mathsf  {T}}\Sigma _3u=1$, bounded because $t_3\ell _3=\tfrac  {369}{625}<1$ and stretched by $\tfrac  {25}{16}$ along $g_3$ alone. Left, downstairs: the deflated design, both of whose vectors are heavy. Right: the three steps of the proof, ending in \eqref  {eq:reassemble} as a sum $X+Y$ of two positive semidefinite matrices. The hypothesis $\ell _3\le 1$ is used once, at the smaller eigenvalue $t_3(1-\ell _3)=\tfrac  {31}{625}$ of $Y$; the other two pairs of this design fail, so the pair the theorem produces is the complement of the light index.}}{40}{figure.20}\protected@file@percent }
