\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {21}{\ignorespaces The pair obstruction \eqref  {eq:obstruction} at $(5,2)$. Left: the squared vectors of an all-heavy design, at distance $\ell _c$ from the origin. The two circles drawn are those of the pair $\{1,3\}$, and the arc on the circle of radius $\ell _3=2$ carries the partners $\eta _d$ with $K_{1d}\le 0$. Every point of that arc makes an angle of at least $\psi ^{*}$ with $\eta _1$, where $\cos \psi ^{*}=\kappa (\ell _c,\ell _d):= \bigl  [(\ell _c-2)(\ell _d-2)-2\bigr  ]/(\ell _c\ell _d)$; both $\kappa +1=2(\ell _c-1)(\ell _d-1)/(\ell _c\ell _d)$ and $1-\kappa =2(\ell _c+\ell _d-1)/(\ell _c\ell _d)$ are positive at a heavy pair, so the arc is proper and nonempty there and the two leverages by themselves decide no pair. Centre: the ten pairs, four of them dominating. Right: the trine of Example\nonbreakingspace \ref {ex:trine2}, where the cosine the design realizes and the threshold $\kappa (2,2)$ are both $-\tfrac  12$, so each pair sits at an endpoint of the arc and $K_{cd}=0$.}}{42}{figure.21}\protected@file@percent }
