\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {37}{\ignorespaces The assembly of \eqref  {eq:statg}--\eqref  {eq:statt}. Left: the passage from a local minimum of $F$ to the system in five steps, each arrow labelled by the rules that license it; the last carries no label, being the comparison of coefficients. Right: the rules. Two give inclusions rather than equalities, (2) and (3), for one reason: $\lambda _{\min }$ is concave and so not Clarke regular where the least eigenvalue is multiple. Both inclusions run the direction a necessary condition needs. The infinitesimal rotations \eqref  {eq:orbit} impose nothing by \eqref  {eq:rotationkill}, so the combination in (2) takes place in a space of dimension $mk+m-k^{2}-1$, which is $14$ at $(6,3)$ and $18$ at $(7,3)$ and is where the bound \eqref  {eq:carath} comes from. Nothing above the rule is formal: \S  \ref {sec:boundaries} carries the whole passage as one of three steps taken on trust, and the ambient library has no Clarke calculus and no $\partial \lambda _{\min }$.}}{77}{figure.37}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:kktassembly}{{37}{77}{The assembly of \eqref {eq:statg}--\eqref {eq:statt}. Left: the passage from a local minimum of $F$ to the system in five steps, each arrow labelled by the rules that license it; the last carries no label, being the comparison of coefficients. Right: the rules. Two give inclusions rather than equalities, (2) and (3), for one reason: $\lmin $ is concave and so not Clarke regular where the least eigenvalue is multiple. Both inclusions run the direction a necessary condition needs. The infinitesimal rotations \eqref {eq:orbit} impose nothing by \eqref {eq:rotationkill}, so the combination in (2) takes place in a space of dimension $mk+m-k^{2}-1$, which is $14$ at $(6,3)$ and $18$ at $(7,3)$ and is where the bound \eqref {eq:carath} comes from. Nothing above the rule is formal: \S \ref {sec:boundaries} carries the whole passage as one of three steps taken on trust, and the ambient library has no Clarke calculus and no $\partial \lmin $}{figure.37}{}}
