\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {40}{\ignorespaces The reach of the exclusions at $(6,3)$. Upper: the census of Proposition\nonbreakingspace \ref {prop:census}, $2102$ covering classes with $351$ of them at $\lvert A^{+}\rvert =10$. Lower, on its own scale: the $34$ classes that Lemma\nonbreakingspace \ref {lem:overlap}(iv) removes for failing to cover, and the $23$ that Proposition\nonbreakingspace \ref {prop:saturated} removes for carrying an index in every member. Only the second sits inside the census, the non-covering classes being absent from it; it takes $1/3$ of the column at $\lvert A^{+}\rvert =3$ and $1/351$ at the peak, and neither exclusion reaches above ten. Both excluded families are graphs on five vertices. The two drawn are the extremes of the $23$, a path beside an edge at three triples and the complete graph at ten. The bars are an external enumeration: neither Proposition\nonbreakingspace \ref {prop:census} nor Proposition\nonbreakingspace \ref {prop:carath} carries a declaration, and only the criteria the panels apply are kernel-checked.}}{87}{figure.40}\protected@file@percent }
