\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {41}{\ignorespaces The nine strategies of this appendix. The third column carries the quantity that refutes each: a determinant leg, a deletion price, an infimum, a $2\times 2$ determinant, a least root, a two-moment discriminant, an inertia, a volume maximizer and a least eigenvalue. The four above the second band fail wherever the selection inequality is an equality; the five below fail at explicit witnesses, none of them through Corollary\nonbreakingspace \ref {cor:nomargin}. Two numbers here are computed in exact rational arithmetic rather than in the kernel: $\delta (C)=-1$ at the maximizer of $\pi _C$, whose gap matrix the development does fix, and $\lvert \det M_C\rvert =12$ at the maximizer of the unweighted volume. The split $20$ and $15$ of the determinant legs at $(7,3)$ is kernel-checked, though not by any declaration tagged on Proposition\nonbreakingspace \ref {prop:noaggregate}.}}{97}{figure.41}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:gallery}{{41}{97}{The nine strategies of this appendix. The third column carries the quantity that refutes each: a determinant leg, a deletion price, an infimum, a $2\times 2$ determinant, a least root, a two-moment discriminant, an inertia, a volume maximizer and a least eigenvalue. The four above the second band fail wherever the selection inequality is an equality; the five below fail at explicit witnesses, none of them through Corollary~\ref {cor:nomargin}. Two numbers here are computed in exact rational arithmetic rather than in the kernel: $\delta (C)=-1$ at the maximizer of $\pi _C$, whose gap matrix the development does fix, and $\lvert \det M_C\rvert =12$ at the maximizer of the unweighted volume. The split $20$ and $15$ of the determinant legs at $(7,3)$ is kernel-checked, though not by any declaration tagged on Proposition~\ref {prop:noaggregate}}{figure.41}{}}
